Variables: name of a memory location which stores some data

Variables Rules:
Varibles are case sensetive mean (a and A are totally different )
1st character shoul be alphabet or("_")
no comma no blank space in Variables name
no other symble other than "_"


Constants

values that dont change(fixed)

Integer constant:1,2,3,-4-5,0
real constant:1.0,2.0,3.14,-2.4
character constant:'a','b','A','#','&'   for character constantwe will single quotes


Keywords: Reserved that has special meaning to the computer 
there are 32 keywords in C:

Program structure:

#include<stdio.h>   (ye line hamesha code me likhni hi likhni hai)

int main (){ isme main function jo hamara code line by line run krta hai
    printf("hello world) is code hmm kabhi bhi change kr skte hai
    return 0;
}


comments : that are not part of are program
single line comment = //
multiple line comment=/* */


Output:
printf("hello world");

new line 
printf("kuch bhi\n")

Output cases:
Integers:
printf("age is %d",age);
Real numbers
printf("value of pi is %f",pi)
Character:
printf("star looks like this %c",star)




